      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The worldwide spread of the coronary heart disease (CHD) epidemic is, in part, related to unfavorable changes in dietary patterns in the developing world. Much has been learned about optimal nutrition for the prevention of CHD. These lessons can, and should, be applied to countries where the burden of CHD is rapidly increasing, in order to help slow the progression of the CHD epidemic, to save many lives, and to prevent considerable disability worldwide."},
